> haha, then the shell game could get REALLY confusing: da se te'ai ve'ai ve
> ve'ai xe se'ai teldunda de di

Assuming that se'ai flips x2 with x2, doing nothing:

se'ai:
  da de di zo'e zo'e
xe:
  zo'e de di zo'e da
ve'ai:
  zo'e zo'e di de da
ve:
  de zo'e di zo'e da
ve'ai:
  de zo'e di zo'e da
te'ai:
  de di zo'e zo'e da
se:
  di de zo'e zo'e da

Which following jvajvo means:
  di gives lock de (which seals something with some locking
characteristics) to recipient da

Makes sense to me!  I'd like to see some posts like that on la
lujyjbo!  Probably off-topic here, though, sorry nintadni. ;)  (At
least it's not more misplaced jbodau!)

